 conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin \\theta(8\\cos \\theta-3\\sin \\theta)-3\\cos^{2}\\theta = 8 \\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta - 3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2519a6-a1d0-5990-b681-0e082f8e2730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sin x \\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556214} {:answer/id #uuid "29030701-4f9c-5697-94e4-7f926abf383b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\sin^{2} x + 6 \\sin x \\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556222} {:answer/id #uuid "2d554715-adf9-5b16-86d4-af3ac0ae8133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556224} {:answer/id #uuid "8e942b4e-595c-57cb-98a4-2dcf7890caee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sin x \\cos x + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556254} {:answer/id #uuid "99b86bbc-42d4-5a73-bfe8-0b81a4a7c8d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sin x \\cos x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99b86bbc-42d4-5a73-bfe8-0b81a4a7c8d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sin x \\cos x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556257} :answer-field/id #uuid "b753164c-0e5a-5ef8-a3fb-a69c038ce571" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556268}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fc06fa2c-e4ba-5f20-956b-c01b1e7bae0d" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\sin x(3\\cos x-2\\sin x)+\\cos x(3\\sin x-2\\cos x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\sin x(3\\cos x-2\\sin x)+\\cos x(3\\sin x-2\\cos x) = 3\\sin x\\cos x-2\\sin^{2}x+3\\sin x\\cos x-2\\cos^{2}x\n$$\n\nNext, we group the $\\sin^2 x$ and $\\cos^2 x$ terms.\n\n$$\n3\\sin x\\cos x-2\\sin^{2}x+3\\sin x\\cos x-2\\cos^{2}x = 6\\sin x\\cos x-2(\\sin^{2}x+\\cos^{2}x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^2{x}+\\cos^2{x}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n6\\sin x\\cos x-2(\\sin^{2}x+\\cos^{2}x) = 6 \\sin x \\cos x - 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin x(3\\cos x-2\\sin x)+\\cos x(3\\sin x-2\\cos x) = 6 \\sin x \\cos x - 2.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Expanding Parentheses and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}]}
